Close the open dependency security advisories (4 Go, 7 JavaScript) (#146)

* fix(deps): bump vite to 7.3.6 and vitest to 3.2.7, closing dev-server security advisories

* fix(deps): upgrade grpc to v1.83.1 and go-jose to v4.1.4

Closes the open Go dependency security advisories: grpc's authorization
bypass via missing leading slash in :path (critical), the xDS RBAC/HTTP-2
vulnerabilities, and the heap-exhaustion OOM via HTTP/2 DATA frame
fragmentation (both high), plus go-jose's JWE decryption panics (high).
v1.83.1 is the minimum grpc version that closes all three grpc advisories
at once; go.mod's transitive go-spiffe requirement was bumped to v2.7.0
by MVS resolution (grpc's own go.mod now requires it). No source changes
were needed.